    <!-- http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Cartoh -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Cartoh">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalCompound"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalSubstance"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCode"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
        <ontology:inchi>1S/C</ontology:inchi>
        <ontology:pubchem>5462310.0</ontology:pubchem>
        <property:inchikey>OKTJSMMVPCPJKN-UHFFFAOYSA-N</property:inchikey>
        <terms:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5462310.0"/>
        <skos:definition>Total humic carbon represents the stable fraction of soil organic matter derived from humified materials. It improves soil structure, nutrient retention, and water-holding capacity, making it critical for long-term soil health and productivity. Source: Stevenson, F.J. (1994). ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/"/>
        <skos:notation>Cartoh</skos:notation>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Carbon (C) - total humic</skos:prefLabel>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon"/>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Cartot -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Cartot">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalCompound"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalSubstance"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCode"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
        <ontology:inchi>1S/C</ontology:inchi>
        <ontology:pubchem>5462310.0</ontology:pubchem>
        <property:inchikey>OKTJSMMVPCPJKN-UHFFFAOYSA-N</property:inchikey>
        <terms:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5462310.0"/>
        <skos:definition>Total carbon in soil includes both organic carbon (from plant and microbial residues) and inorganic carbon (primarily carbonates). It is a fundamental component of soil organic matter, influencing soil fertility, structure, and water retention. High carbon levels are associated with better soil health and productivity. Source: USDA NRCS. ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/"/>
        <skos:notation>Cartot</skos:notation>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Carbon (C) - total</skos:prefLabel>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon"/>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Ccetot -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Ccetot">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalCompound"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalSubstance"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCode"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
        <ontology:inchi>1S/CH2O3.Ca/c2-1(3)4;/h(H2,2,3,4);/q;+2/p-2</ontology:inchi>
        <ontology:pubchem>10112.0</ontology:pubchem>
        <property:inchikey>VTYYLEPIZMXCLO-UHFFFAOYSA-L</property:inchikey>
        <terms:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/10112.0"/>
        <skos:definition>The total calcium carbonate equivalent measures the full capacity of soil to neutralize acidity, considering all forms of carbonate and bicarbonate minerals. It is essential for managing soil pH and nutrient availability in acidic soils. Source: FAO Soil Bulletin. ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/"/>
        <skos:notation>Ccetot</skos:notation>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Calcium carbonate equivalent - total</skos:prefLabel>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon"/>
        <ssn:isPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


